equests":1},"project.symbol-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":61998.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":2158.0,"requests":5}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the last-sweep stamp lifecycle: who writes it, when (after a successful sweep, not at start), where (.rebar/), and how its write is coordinated with the advisory lock so a crashed sweep does not leave a falsely-fresh stamp.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T7","T9"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1722,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'OR a last-sweep stamp is older than a configured interval (one stat). The stamp check is what makes it a real floor'","No CREATE/UPDATE path stated for the stamp — only the CONSUME (stat) side is described","If nothing writes the stamp, the staleness arm fires on every close and storms; if it writes at start rather than after a successful fold, a crashed sweep leaves it fresh and suppresses the floor"],"finding":"The last-sweep stamp's create/update lifecycle is unspecified: the plan describes CONSUMING it (a stat for staleness in the O(1) floor check) but never states who writes/updates it, when (sweep start vs successful completion), or how its write is coordinated across the detached worker and the CI/disposable-runner sweeps.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa7f16bdc52d130d0","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section 3 (Operation-linked fallback) — 'a last-sweep stamp is older than a configured interval (one stat)'","norm_id":"nbc9b60c6f8138dcb","priority":0.7778,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["The detached worker crashes before folding; the stamp was written at start, so the floor stays quiet and no ticket ever folds","Two clones both see a stale stamp and both spawn — advisory lock gates the fold but the stamp write ordering across them is undefined"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State that the sweep worker writes the stamp only after the fold+push completes, under the same advisory lock, and that the CI sweep updates the same tickets-branch-independent local stamp; add an AC that a crashed pre-fold worker leaves the stamp stale so the floor re-fires.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Place the close-path compaction trigger in the shared close engine seam (the close *_core / _seam.append_event completion path) rather than only in transition_close.py, so MCP and library closes inherit the out-of-band floor.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.engine-layer-enforcement"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2333,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Operation-linked fallback — the floor that works everywhere. On the close path, AFTER the store lock is released and after the best-effort push...'","Scope: 'src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py — call the trigger after the push.'","rebar reaches close through CLI, MCP tool handlers, and the library transition facade; only the CLI command file is named as the trigger call site."],"finding":"The operation-linked fallback — described as 'the floor that works everywhere' — is hooked into transition_close.py, the CLI close command. Ticket close is also reachable via the MCP server and the library transition facade; if those reach the same close without passing through the CLI command's post-push trigger call, closing via MCP or library never triggers out-of-band compaction, defeating the stated universal floor.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2493392097b44c49","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section 3 and Scope: 'src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py — call the trigger after the push.'","norm_id":"n016dc5bea6a119d6","priority":0.6667,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["An adopter closing a ticket via the MCP server tool never spawns the detached compaction worker, so the 'floor that works everywhere' does not fire — event logs grow unbounded exactly as before.","A library consumer calling rebar.transition(...) to close bypasses the CLI command's post-push trigger, so out-of-band compaction never triggers for library-only integrations."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Hook the trigger into whatever shared core function all three close ingress paths call after releasing the store lock, or explicitly confirm transition_close.py is that shared seam.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"insufficient","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"insufficient","impact_follows_necessarily":"insufficient","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"insufficient","path_reachable":"insufficient","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State explicitly how Windows-with-no-CI adopters get standing compaction (e.g. an inline synchronous fold path on the close for Windows, or a documented required manual/CI step), so the 'works everywhere' floor is not silently absent on Windows.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3137,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Windows is a v1 no-op, mirroring the drain, because the store lock's fcntl import would crash a detached child.'","'compaction must also work with no CI and no local cron — that is why the original design was linked to an operation'","Platform matrix cell: Windows developer workstation."],"finding":"The 'floor that works everywhere' does not work on Windows: the plan makes the detached-spawn trigger a v1 no-op on Windows (mirroring the drain) because fcntl would crash the detached child. Combined with the CI-only scheduled sweep, a Windows developer workstation with no CI has no out-of-band compaction trigger at all — the very gap the plan sets out to close.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f38b95e4fddd5e114","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section 3: 'Windows is a v1 no-op, mirroring the drain, because the store lock's fcntl import would crash a detached child.'","norm_id":"n5eab453cc89a2d9b","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["Windows platform, developer workstation, no CI: closing tickets never triggers the detached worker (v1 no-op) and there is no scheduled sweep, so event logs grow unbounded until the user manually runs `rebar compact` — the exact starvation the plan claims to fix, now unfixed on Windows."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Provide a Windows-safe synchronous inline fold (reusing the 'always' knob path) on the close trigger, or scope the plan's universality claim to POSIX and document the Windows manual/CI requirement.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the default value for the new sweep-interval config key (e.g. mirror the 6h cron) so the floor's staleness threshold is not left to the executor.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T7","T9"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.536,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'a last-sweep stamp is older than a configured interval'","No default interval value stated anywhere in Approach, Scope, or Acceptance Criteria","Contrast: the horizon default (30 min) and compact.threshold are explicitly cited with defaults"],"finding":"The new sweep-interval config key has no stated default value. The 6h cron and the reused compact.threshold defaults are given, but the interval that gates the operation-linked floor's stamp check is only described as 'a configured interval' with no default, leaving the executor to invent one.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb75924f7518bb63c","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope — 'src/rebar/_config_schema.py — the tri-state knob and the sweep interval'","norm_id":"n6a99ae67dd2d2d22","priority":0.264,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["Executor picks an interval that is too short (storms) or too long (floor effectively disabled)"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Set the interval default to align with the 6h scheduled cadence so the floor is a genuine backstop rather than a primary trigger.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes"